Azure DNS

Azure DNS is a service that lets you host and manage your domain names using Azure.

Key Points:
            Translates domain names → IP addresses
            Uses Azure’s global infrastructure for high availability
            Faster and more reliable name resolution

How It Works:
              You create a DNS zone (e.g. myapp.com)
              Add DNS records (like A, CNAME, MX)
              Azure answers DNS queries for your domain

Common Record Types:
                    A record → maps a name to an IP address
                    CNAME → maps one domain to another
                    MX → email servers
                    TXT → verification and metadata

Benefits:
          High performance using Azure network
          Easy to manage via Azure portal
          Integrates with other Azure services

Use Cases:
          Host public domain names
          Route users to your applications
          Manage DNS for cloud apps
